# Task 16: R-10 trimesh.facets cross-check diagnostic in tests
## Evidence log — 2026-08-05

### Baseline (unchanged tree)
```
py -3.14 -m pytest tests/ -k "not live" -q
219 passed, 18 deselected in 17.38s
```

### Changes (NEW files only — no production code touched)
- `tests/trimesh_facets_diag.py` (NEW): test-only helper
  `_compare_with_trimesh_facets(decompose_result, mesh: trimesh.Trimesh)`.
  Runs `mesh.facets` (trimesh's parallel-adjacency components built on the
  curvature-adaptive ratio predicate `(radius/span)^2 > 5000`,
  `tol.facet_threshold == 5000`, `min_len=2` — verified against installed
  trimesh 5.0.0 source `trimesh/graph.py`), maps every facet's triangles
  onto our `planar_faces` by plane-offset + centroid-in-polygon containment,
  and reports discrepancies (a facet not covered by exactly one of our
  faces). Returns a report dict {our_face_count, trimesh_facet_count,
  invariant_ok, facets_error, facet_sizes, our_face_triangle_counts,
  single_face_analogues, plane_facet_groups, discrepancies,
  discrepancy_count} and emits `warnings.warn` diagnostics. Never raises:
  `mesh.facets` failures on degenerate input are caught and surfaced as
  `report["facets_error"]`.
  - Edge cases documented + handled gracefully:
    - trimesh issue #347 (single-face facets): trimesh's `facets` uses
      `connected_components(min_len=2)`, so a facet of one face is NEVER
      emitted. Our decompose DOES emit single-triangle planar faces; those
      are counted as `single_face_analogues` (expected, logged).
    - trimesh issue #1745 (splitting with faces on a plane): facets sharing
      one plane are counted as `plane_facet_groups` (expected, logged).
- `tests/test_trimesh_facets_cross_check.py` (NEW): 5 tests
  - `test_trimesh_facets_cross_check` — unit cube: 6 planar faces, 6
    trimesh facets (sizes all 2), invariant `our >= trimesh` holds,
    zero discrepancies, diagnostic summary warning emitted.
  - `test_trimesh_facets_cross_check_single_face_facet_347` — lone
    triangle + quad: trimesh drops the single-face facet (1 facet), our
    decompose emits 2 faces, `single_face_analogues == 1`, #347 warning.
  - `test_trimesh_facets_cross_check_faces_on_plane_1745` — two separated
    coplanar quads on z=0: 2 facets sharing a plane,
    `plane_facet_groups >= 1`, #1745 warning.
  - `test_trimesh_facets_cross_check_degenerate_graceful` — all-collinear:
    both sides report 0, invariant holds, no crash.
  - `test_trimesh_facets_cross_check_facets_error_graceful` — monkeypatches
    `mesh.facets` (via `property(_boom)`) to raise: helper catches, reports
    `facets_error`, emits warning, returns report, no exception propagates.

### Debugging note (kept in code as comments)
Initial coverage matcher used only the dominant-axis 2D projection — parallel
faces at different offsets (cube z=0 vs z=1) project identically, so every
facet matched 2 faces (6 discrepancies). Fixed with a plane-offset check
`|n·centroid − n·poly[0]| <= max(1e-4, 1e-6*|offset|)` in
`_face_covering_indices`.

